# ALUS character descriptions (sr).
# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
#
# Format: character<TAB>description[<TAB>further description...]
# Taken from NVDA source/locale/sr/characterDescriptions.dic, which is the
# same data a user of NVDA already knows by ear.
#Serbian characterDescriptions.dic
#A part of NonVisual Desktop Access (NVDA)
#URL: https://www.nvda-project.org/
#
# Both scripts, each describing itself: a Latin key gets a Latin mnemonic and a
# Cyrillic key a Cyrillic one. That matters for braille rather than for speech
# -- a Serbian voice reads either script the same way, but sr-Cyrl.ctb does
# not, so a Cyrillic mnemonic under a Latin key would come out as the wrong
# cells. ALUS changed exactly one line of the inherited file for that reason:
# `x` had a Cyrillic mnemonic among Latin ones.


